{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox","id":1098835,"title":"Explain to a noob: Sidereal Paradox","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T12:12:54-07:00","id":1098835,"title":"Explain to a noob: Sidereal Paradox","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> I'm currently ST'ing a game in which Sidereals make semi-frequent appearances, often as Resplendid Destinies.<br /> Now, I've glanced at the Sidereal's book for Second Edition, and I think I understand most of the stuff, but not Paradox.<br /> Or rather, I understand the basic concept, but not why it's considered so bad. Everywhere I read about Sidereals, people mention how bad they consider paradox.<br /> I'm sure that given time and experience I'll understand why it's bad, but I need to correctly ST a Sidereal for the time being, so... why does the internet think Paradox is a bad mechanic? What was so bad about it?<br /> <br /> Many thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:16:04-07:00","id":1098836,"title":"","content":"To clarify, are you asking why Sidereal would consider Paradox a bad thing to be avoided, or are you asking why the community considers Paradox to be a bad mechanic to have in the game in general?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:19:08-07:00","id":1098838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098836#post1098836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify, are you asking why Sidereal would consider Paradox a bad thing to be avoided, or are you asking why the community considers Paradox to be a bad mechanic to have in the game in general?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter. I understand Paradox is a &quot;negative&quot; mechanic, but why is it's inclusion bad for the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:32:53-07:00","id":1098842,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there's a bunch of other backlogged negative feelings deeply embedded in the culture, but the primary issue I've taken with it that I've seen echoed elsewhere is the ability of the game to outright murder your background (or even your character) for interacting with the mechanics. If I knew that someone I cared about could die, or that I could just straight up take more damage that I have life, I would be pretty reluctant to gain any Paradox.<br /> <br /> To that end, in most cases the carrot was not juicy enough to justify the stick. Astrology offers a lot of potential for Paradox, but it was cooler in concept than practice in most cases. Punishment mechanics suck. You should always be trying to encourage players to do interesting things. That's my 2 cents, (before this turns into a Limit conversation) hope it helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:39:05-07:00","id":1098846,"title":"","content":"It helps, thanks. The difference between Paradox and Limit would be that Paradox takes away from the story (by killing NPC's or even your character) while Limit Break should add to it (even in a less pleasant way), then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:46:55-07:00","id":1098848,"title":"","content":"Even if we ignore the possibility of the Pattern Spiders potentially outright murdering you on a random dice roll... which is pretty shitty even by the standards of punishments imposed by the Yozis and the Neverborn. Most of the outcomes end up as &quot;don't do anything for d10 days&quot; and the only canonical way to burn it off is via the rituals that similarly consist of your character not doing anything. Factor in the fact Astrology tends to be really weak when you're not inviting Censure it feels a bit needless.<br /> <br /> Astrology charms use Paradox cost well, but that doesn't change that the basic situation is off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:56:32-07:00","id":1098850,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the problem with Paradox was that it was so harsh. Sure, some of the options on the roll weren't too bad. Suffer a -3 would penalty for 1-10 weeks is harsh, but livable. Being reduced to zero Appearance for 1-10 months sucks, but again it's not necessarily game over.<br /> <br /> But lose all motes and can't regain motes for 1-10 days? So you don't get to use Charms? What is your character supposed to do if you end up in a fight? Or how about losing your ability to perform Combos, which under the 2nd edition paradigm was a death sentence? Losing all Willpower, again, meant no combo's. Even something seemingly minor like Falling into a coma for 1-10 days is terrible. If the PC's need to stop Raksi's plan in 3 days, but your character is in a coma for the next 7 days, you're in trouble, and your ST will either have to handwave things, ask you to sit out of the next session, or have you play an NPC character instead. And, of course, Essence Venom is potentially just an auto-kill effect if you roll high on the damage and don't have Ox Bodies or a high Stamina.<br /> <br /> Roughly half of the Paradox effects would either directly require the PC to sit out of the game for a time, or would basically force the PC to do that. These effects were not &quot;fun&quot; or &quot;interesting&quot; or &quot;engaging.&quot; They were just Fuck You effects.<br /> <br /> The only other Exalted type with something similar was Abyssals with their Resonance. But if the big difference is, the player was allowed to choose which Resonance their character would suffer from. So if they didn't want a particular Resonance effect, or if that Resonance effect would have an intensely negative impact on the play experience, the player could just not select that effect. While Resonance had problems, Paradox was much worse in every respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:08:51-07:00","id":1098855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098838#post1098838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter. I understand Paradox is a &quot;negative&quot; mechanic, but why is it's inclusion bad for the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, most of it is this fandom's usual propensity for throwing the baby out with the bathwater.<br /> <br /> That's not to say Paradox is a good mechanic as-is. It's overly punitive, which feels particularly bad and unwarranted since Astrology that causes it is neither that powerful nor that fun to use even without the added disincentive. It's also pretty random, which many people feel clashes with the themes of the Sidereal Exalted. With Sids being the hubristic manipulators, you'd think Paradox is about their meddling in the Loom causing unwanted tangles in the tapestry in a way that's directly relevant to what they were meddling in, not unlike what botches do to sorcerous workings. But no, it's Pattern Spiders getting pissed at you for daring to increase their workload and biting your fate strand to make a random horrible thing happen to you. Clearly you can see the wasted potential here.<br /> <br /> But that's the thing - the idea has potential, and if handled properly (and coupled with otherwise more inviting Astrology mechanics), would make a great tool for adding interesting complications to a story involving fate manipulation. I agree what we have in previous editions is pretty weak and you're probably better off not using it should you choose to play either of them, but I don't think the idea should be scrapped from the game entirely, at least not without attempting to remold it into something useful and fun first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:14:48-07:00","id":1098858,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the really shitty thing about Paradox is that it essentially ended up punishing the player, not the character, often by removing (or effectively removing, see Anubis' point re: motes), and didn't even do so in a particularly interesting way. And that's not even getting into how that's all in-character time; so your character is in the coma for five days? Too bad you zonked out just before the siege of the city started and those five days will take six sessions to play out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098848#post1098848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Factor in the fact Astrology tends to be really weak when you're not inviting Censure it feels a bit needless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astrology is pretty damn weak even when you <i>are</i> inviting censure, considering that you potentially risk it when using Astrology on anything larger than a standard adventuring party or small fishing village.<br /> <br /> And that's also not getting into all the other problems with Astrology (generally more efficient to use as power batteries, moderate level specalization to use, Colleges one of the lowest investment-to-benefit returns in the game, no one knows what the fuck it actually does, etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:25:56-07:00","id":1098866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098855#post1098855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the idea should be scrapped from the game entirely, at least not without attempting to remold it into something useful and fun first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall ever hearing people claiming that Paradox as an idea was bad. Just that the implementation of it was. And, yeah, as people have noted... The Paradox Effects <i>aren't fun</i>. They don't really contribute to a good story, which in some ways is worse than them being harsh.<br /> <br /> Like, a curse of &quot;You respire Motes at 5 every TWO hours outside of combat, until you find and apologize to the God who laid it&quot;, THAT can be worked into a story. That can lead to potential events and some fun.<br /> <br /> Just &quot;Welp you can't respire Essence for 1d10 days&quot; means either your Sidereal has to go sit on the couch for a week and change, potentially missing out on some sessions, or it'll lead to the ST saying &quot;... Right let's just skip forward a month&quot;. Nothing's really gained with the latter, and the former... Well few things suck more at a game session than &quot;Sorry but my character isn't there... I guess I'll pull out my DS or something, don't worry about me&quot;. These DON'T lend themselves well to enriching the play experience.<br /> <br /> That said... Well we don't know what form Paradox will take come the Sidereals book in this new edition. I'm moderately curious, since I actually don't mind some of the changes made to Limit Break. (I don't really LIKE Limit Break and when I play in games that don't use it I don't feel as though I'm missing anything, but I don't HATE it)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:27:02-07:00","id":1098868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098858#post1098858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astrology is pretty damn weak even when you <i>are</i> inviting censure, considering that you potentially risk it when using Astrology on anything larger than a standard adventuring party or small fishing village.<br /> <br /> And that's also not getting into all the other problems with Astrology (generally more efficient to use as power batteries, moderate level specalization to use, Colleges one of the lowest investment-to-benefit returns in the game, no one knows what the fuck it actually does, etc)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually talking about the power battery effects there. RAW the Hound-Chases Rabbit Blessing willpower shenanigans invite censure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:32:00-07:00","id":1098869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098866#post1098866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall ever hearing people claiming that Paradox as an idea was bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure I've seen it come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T13:42:39-07:00","id":1098873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098866#post1098866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, a curse of &quot;You respire Motes at 5 every TWO hours outside of combat, until you find and apologize to the God who laid it&quot;, THAT can be worked into a story. That can lead to potential events and some fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>My last Sidereal would probably more go the route of &quot;Laying a kung-fu smackdown on them and then bringing them up on charges including but not limited to treason, willful obstruction of official Bureau of Destiny business and being insufficinently humble&quot;...but, ya'know, different strokes and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said... Well we don't know what form Paradox will take come the Sidereals book in this new edition. I'm moderately curious, since I actually don't mind some of the changes made to Limit Break. (I don't really LIKE Limit Break and when I play in games that don't use it I don't feel as though I'm missing anything, but I don't HATE it) </div> </div> </div>Vance and Minton are at least aware of the problems of Astrology and Paradox, if for no other reason than I know they've participated in threads where I was doing some heavy grousing about them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098868#post1098868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually talking about the power battery effects there. RAW the Hound-Chases Rabbit Blessing willpower shenanigans invite censure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, for some reason I thought you were referring to general use Astrology, as in the blessings and curses. My mistake.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T19:39:23-07:00","id":1098995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098869#post1098869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure I've seen it come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>See this is why I try not to make many absolute claims. I'm hardly omniscient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098873#post1098873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My last Sidereal would probably more go the route of &quot;Laying a kung-fu smackdown on them and then bringing them up on charges including but not limited to treason, willful obstruction of official Bureau of Destiny business and being insufficinently humble&quot;...but, ya'know, different strokes and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And still leads to a fun little plotline on the side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T20:27:11-07:00","id":1099004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098869#post1098869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure I've seen it come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure it has. People say all sorts of stuff. For the most part though, I think most people on the forum have the attitude that Paradox as a hyper-punishing mechanic for using Astrology was a terrible idea, and that if Exalted 3rd edition wants to include Paradox as a mechanic for Sidereals in 3rd edition, it needs to radically rethink both Astrology as a system and mechanic, as well as what how they want Paradox to add to the game.<br /> <br /> And for a lot of people, just getting rid of it and coming up with something entirely fresh is the best thing to do. And to be honest, I can't blame them. Holding on to prior ideas purely out of a sense of nostalgia or such isn't really a good idea. Hang on to those ideas only if doing so can be done in a way that will truly make the game better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:03:27-07:00","id":1099051,"title":"","content":"It's in a similar vein to Resonance, in that it almost seemed designed to make play unfun, and could be used as a railroading mechanic. I agree that it needs to be totally rethought if it's going to work as a worthwhile concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1165-hecaton","name":"Hecaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T04:17:25-07:00","id":1099107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1098835-explain-to-a-noob-sidereal-paradox?p=1098858#post1098858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no one knows what the fuck it actually does</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI like the idea Grabowski once laid out about the idea of Fate as a means of conditioning certain patterns of behaviour via circumstantial benefits or impediments, but if that kind of thing was the intent, it would definitely need to be laid out more explicitly.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut even considering that, it touches on one of my own issues, namely the purpose of specifying mechanics such as this for things that are happening off-scene.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's a matter that I think about any time something comes up based on providing bonuses or even actual powers to characters who are probably mostly going to be doing things with them outside of the main action with the players, which raises the question of exactly how to arbitrate them.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike, if you change the target number for some character and then leave, is the Storyteller supposed to intermittently make secret dice rolls for that character corresponding to what they're presumably doing elsewhere, and keep the results in mind for plot hooks if they ever come back into the action? If you use Prophet-Uplifting Evocation on somebody, should the Storyteller be imagining scenarios in which their Defining Principle comes under attack and they spend some of the motes they were given to bolster it? Or does it all just exist in a space of &quot;resolve through mechanics when they're in the scene, and at all other times just vaguely assume that things fitting the spirit of the effect occur&quot;?<br /> <br /> \u200bMore than providing some kind of resolution on this, I think there are a few too many effects that provide specific mechanical bonuses for characters who are almost definitely going to then leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}